>
> "X thinks that Y likes Z"
>
> as an example of ternary (three-argument) relation. That isn't how "to
> think that ..." is commonly represented with a Lojban selbri:

You can always define a selbri in Lojban with any place structure you
want. For example:

nelji'i: ko'a jinvi lo du'u ko'e nelci ko'i kei ko'e jo'u ko'i (ko'o)
         "x1 thinks that x2 likes x3 (on grounds x4)"

mu'o mi'e xorxes

